  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the rice in a fine strainer until the water runs mostly clear. Set it aside to drain.",
    "Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes, until soft and lightly golden.",
    "Stir in the garlic, ginger, turmeric, and cumin. Cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the lentils, tomatoes with their juice, 4 cups of the water, and the salt. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat to a simmer.",
    "Simmer uncovered for 18 to 20 minutes, stirring often, until the lentils fall apart and the dal is thick. Add a splash of water if it gets too thick.",
    "While the dal cooks, combine the rice and the remaining 1 cup water... in a separate covered saucepan is not needed: instead, stir the drained rice into the dal after 8 minutes of simmering, add 1 more cup of water if the pot looks dry, and keep simmering.",
    "Cook until the rice is tender and the lentils are creamy, about 12 more minutes. Stir often so nothing sticks to the bottom.",
    "Stir in the lemon juice and taste for salt. Rest the pot off the heat for 5 minutes, then serve."
  ],
